ndition characterized by an inadequate or unbalanced intake of nutrients, which can lead to various complications and negatively impact the quality of life. It is particularly prevalent among cancer patients, where it manifests as weight loss, decreased muscle mass, and diminished strength, complicating treatment and recovery. This condition can arise from several factors, including chronic diseases such as cancer, renal insufficiency, liver disease, and conditions like dysphagia, which hinder proper nutrient intake.\n\nIn cancer patients, malnutrition is a common diagnosis, affecting approximately 80% of those with advanced gastric cancer and leading to poor health outcomes and increased mortality rates. It can also complicate recovery in patients undergoing surgical procedures and those receiving treatments like hematopoietic cell transplantation. Nutritional deficiencies in these patients can result in a weakened immune response, prolonged hospital stays, and a greater risk of complications.\n\nMalnutrition is not limited to cancer patients; it is also a critical issue among the elderly, particularly those in palliative care, where it can lead to functional and social incapacity. In geriatric patients, malnutrition may necessitate nutritional support interventions to improve health outcomes. Additionally, malnutrition can occur in patients with chronic kidney disease, liver disease, and other conditions, often requiring specialized dietary considerations and interventions, such as parenteral nutrition.\n\nOverall, malnutrition encompasses both undernutrition and overnutrition, affecting health and well-being across various populations. It is essential to recognize and address malnutrition through appropriate nutritional assessments and interventions to enhance recovery and quality of life for affected individuals.\",104\r\n7130,DEFICIT DE ZINC,\"El déficit de zinc es una alteración que puede contribuir a la malnutrición en pacientes con enfermedad hepática crónica. En el caso de un paciente específico, se detectó el déficit de zinc durante los controles evolutivos, lo que llevó a abordar este problema mediante la administración de suplementos.\",2\r\n571,ENFERMEDAD AGUDA,\"\"\"ENFERMEDAD AGUDA\"\" refers to any acute illness or psychological stress experienced by a patient within the last three months. This condition can significantly impact the patient's nutritional status and overall health. Acute illnesses often lead to increased nutritional needs, which are crucial for recovery and maintaining health. The effects of \"\"enfermedad aguda\"\" are evaluated through tools such as the Mini Nutritional Assessment, which helps in assessing the nutritional implications of recent acute illnesses or psychological stress on the patient.\",2\r\n13407,CÁNCER GASTROINTESTINAL,\"Cancer affecting the gastrointestinal tract, which has low survival rates and requires careful nutritional management.\",3\r\n1861,FÍSTULAS,\"Fístulas are abnormal connections between organs that can lead to complications in nutrition, potentially causing nutrient loss and affecting the patient's overall nutritional status. These abnormal connections may necessitate enteral feeding to ensure adequate nutrient intake. In certain cases, fístulas can benefit from enteral feeding if the access route is appropriately adjusted to accommodate the condition.\",2\r\n56,AISLAMIENTO,\"AISLAMIENTO refers to the phenomenon of isolation, which is a prevalent issue particularly among the elderly population. This isolation can have detrimental effects on their nutritional habits, as social interactions are often linked to eating and meal preparation. Additionally, isolation serves as a social consequence that can significantly impact patients suffering from dysphagia, a condition characterized by difficulties in swallowing. For these individuals, the challenges associated with eating can be exacerbated by a lack of social support and interaction, further complicating their nutritional intake and overall well-being.\",2\r\n2404,POLIFARMACIA,\"Polifarmacia, also known as polypharmacy, is characterized by the concurrent use of five or more medications by an individual, particularly among the elderly population. This practice can significantly impact nutrient absorption and metabolism, potentially leading to adverse health outcomes. Additionally, the use of multiple medications can contribute to frailty in older adults, highlighting the importance of careful management and monitoring of medication regimens in this demographic.\",2\r\n1713,CAMBIOS EN LA INGESTA DIETÉTICA,Changes in dietary intake can affect nutritional status and are important to assess in evaluations.,1\r\n1711,CAPACIDAD FUNCIONAL,\"Functional capacity refers to a patient's ability to perform daily activities, which can impact nutritional status.\",1\r\n12375,CRECIMIENTO,\"Proceso biológico que puede requerir un aumento en la ingesta nutricional, especialmente en niños y adolescentes\",1\r\n13393,CRIBADO MUST,El cribado MUST (Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool) es una herramienta utilizada para evaluar la malnutrición y su impacto en la morbilidad postoperatoria.,1\r\n15281,DESNUTRICIÓN AGUDA GRAVE,Severe acute malnutrition is a life-threatening condition that occurs when a child is extremely thin for their height or has nutritional edema.,1\r\n15280,DESNUTRICIÓN AGUDA MODERADA,\"Moderate acute malnutrition is a condition characterized by a significant weight loss or low weight-for-height in children, indicating a serious health risk.\",1\r\n15283,DESNUTRICIÓN CRÓNICA GRAVE,Severe chronic malnutrition is a serious condition where a child is significantly shorter than the average for their age due to prolonged nutritional deficiencies.,1\r\n15282,DESNUTRICIÓN CRÓNICA MODERADA,\"Moderate chronic malnutrition is characterized by low height-for-age, indicating long-term nutritional deficiencies.\",1\r\n2410,DETERIORO COGNITIVO,Cognitive decline is a common issue in the elderly that can be exacerbated by malnutrition.,1\r\n13391,DUODENOPANCREATECTOMÍA CEFÁLICA,La duodenopancreatectomía cefálica es un procedimiento quirúrgico estándar para el tratamiento de tumores en la cabeza del páncreas y tiene complicaciones nutricionales significativas.,1\r\n2412,ENFERMO,,1\r\n1714,ESTRÉS PSICOLÓGICO,\"Psychological stress can impact a patient's nutritional intake and overall health, making it a relevant factor in assessments.\",1\r\n16339,ESTUDIO ESPAÑOL DE 2007,A study conducted in Spain in 2007 that evaluated the costs associated with nutritional support for malnourished patients.,1\r\n2411,HIPOTENSIÓN POSTURAL,\"Postural hypotension is a condition where blood pressure drops significantly upon standing, often affecting the elderly.\",1\r\n2256,SUPLEMENTOS CALÓRICOS,Adiciones a la dieta recomendadas para pacientes con malnutrición o retraso del crecimiento en la enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal.,1\r\n2403,PLURIPATOLOGÍA,\"Pluripatología refers to the presence of multiple diseases that affect the nutrition of the elderly, particularly chronic and psychiatric conditions.\",1\r\n2405,POBREZA,Poverty is a cause of nutritional deficits and associated diseases in the elderly.,1\r\n2409,SÍNDROMES GERIÁTRICOS,\"SÍNDROMES GERIÁTRICOS refers to a group of clinical conditions that commonly affect the elderly population. These syndromes include delirium, falls, immobility, incontinence, and pressure ulcers, all of which are associated with frailty in older adults. Geriatric syndromes are often interrelated with malnutrition and other health issues, highlighting the complex health challenges faced by this demographic.\",1\r\n13394,ÍNDICE DE RIESGO NUTRICIONAL,El Índice de Riesgo Nutricional (IRN) es una herramienta que muestra concordancia en relación con la morbilidad global en pacientes con cáncer.,1\r\n13408,QUIMIO Y/O RADIOTERAPIA,Chemotherapy and/or radiotherapy are treatments that can complicate the nutritional status of patients with gastrointestinal