l nutrition is used when enteral nutrition is inadequate for patients with gastrointestinal cancer,441\r\n2690,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,MALNUTRICIÓN,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a medical intervention that is frequently employed to address MALNUTRICIÓN, particularly in patients who are unable to consume food orally. This form of nutrition is especially recommended for patients experiencing malnutrition who are undergoing surgical procedures. By providing essential nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract, enteral nutrition plays a crucial role in the management and treatment of malnutrition in various clinical settings.\",439\r\n2826,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,FÍSTULAS,\"Las fístulas pueden complicar la nutrición enteral, pero en ciertos casos, se puede ajustar la fórmula y la vía de acceso para permitir su uso.\",337\r\n586,PACIENTES,MALNUTRICIÓN,\"Los pacientes, especialmente aquellos con cáncer de esófago, a menudo enfrentan problemas de malnutrición. Esta condición se debe principalmente a la pérdida de peso y a la disminución de la ingesta de alimentos. Además, los pacientes que están en riesgo de síndrome de realimentación también experimentan malnutrición, lo que agrava su estado de salud. En conjunto, estas situaciones resaltan la vulnerabilidad de los pacientes a la malnutrición, que puede ser un factor crítico en su tratamiento y recuperación.\",331\r\n354,DISFAGIA,MALNUTRICIÓN,Dysphagia can lead to malnutrition due to difficulties in swallowing food,257\r\n1693,SARCOPENIA,MALNUTRICIÓN,\"Sarcopenia and malnutrition are closely interconnected, particularly in patients with cirrhosis. Malnutrition in these patients encompasses sarcopenia, which is characterized by a reduction in muscle mass and strength. Inadequate nutrition significantly contributes to the development of sarcopenia, highlighting the importance of addressing nutritional deficiencies to mitigate muscle loss in affected individuals.\",187\r\n6997,CÁNCER,MALNUTRICIÓN,\"Cancer and malnutrition are closely interconnected, with malnutrition being a prevalent issue among cancer patients. This condition arises due to various factors associated with the disease, including metabolic changes, treatment side effects, and reduced food intake. Malnutrition not only complicates the treatment and recovery of cancer patients but also significantly impacts patient outcomes and the overall efficacy of cancer therapies. Furthermore, malnutrition can serve as a risk factor in the development of cancer, highlighting the importance of addressing nutritional needs in cancer care to improve patient health and treatment success.\",170\r\n7251,MALNUTRICIÓN,PROTEÍNAS,\"MALNUTRICIÓN and PROTEÍNAS are closely interconnected, particularly in the context of patients with renal insufficiency. Malnutrition in these patients is frequently associated with inadequate protein consumption, which can significantly impact their overall health. Furthermore, malnutrition influences protein metabolism, and this relationship is evaluated through nitrogen balance, a measure that reflects both protein intake and excretion. This highlights the critical role of adequate protein levels in maintaining health and managing malnutrition in individuals with renal issues.\",161\r\n6950,ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL,MALNUTRICIÓN,\"La malnutrición es una consecuencia común de la enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal, afectando la salud general del paciente\",161\r\n7282,MALNUTRICIÓN,CIRROSIS,\"La cirrosis está asociada con la malnutrición, que es una de sus complicaciones más frecuentes\",158\r\n260,DISFAGIA,AISLAMIENTO,Isolation can occur as a social consequence for individuals suffering from dysphagia,155\r\n6859,INSUFICIENCIA RENAL,MALNUTRICIÓN,La insuficiencia renal puede llevar a la malnutrición debido a la ingesta inadecuada de nutrientes y otros factores,145\r\n7268,MALNUTRICIÓN,DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2,\"Malnutrition is prevalent among patients with Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2, impacting their health outcomes\",14